      "tags": ["Chicken", "Quick & Easy", "Family Favorite"],
      "instructions": "1. Mix curry powder, coconut milk, sugar, and salt. Toss chicken thigh pieces in the marinade and thread onto skewers.\n2. For the sauce, whisk peanut butter, soy sauce, lime juice, brown sugar, and a splash of boiling water until smooth.\n3. Heat a grill or large pan over medium-high heat with a little oil.\n4. Cook the chicken skewers for 3-4 minutes per side until charred and cooked through.\n5. Serve skewers hot with the creamy peanut sauce for dipping.",
