      "tags": ["Korean", "Soup", "Spicy", "Quick & Easy"],
      "instructions": "1. In a pot, bring chicken broth, minced garlic, soy sauce, and Gochujang (Korean chili paste) to a boil.\n2. Add dried ramen noodles (discard the seasoning packets) and cook for 2 minutes.\n3. Drop in a cracked egg and let it poach in the boiling broth for 1 minute.\n4. Remove from heat, stir in a drizzle of sesame oil and chopped green onions.\n5. Serve immediately while piping hot.",
